From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:33:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [zlib][x86] Enable AVX-512 CRC-32 in the GN build

The AVX-512/VPCLMULQDQ CRC-32 kernel has been in Chromium zlib since
https://crrev.com/c/4374529 but is only compiled for CMake builds. With
the CPU and OS checks from the parent CL it is selected at runtime only
when AVX-512F, VPCLMULQDQ and the matching XCR0 state are present; other
CPUs keep the SSE4.2/PCLMUL path. The kernel is compiled through its
function target attribute, so no other code gets AVX-512 instructions.
Clang and GCC (since https://crrev.com/c/8309425) both build it.

zlib_bench, AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (Zen 4), Windows x64, clang-cl 21 with
the GN x64 defines, snappy testdata plus a 23 MiB PE, median of 5
interleaved rounds, geomean over 12 files, MB/s:

                    gzip comp  gzip decomp  zlib comp  zlib decomp
  SSE4.2 (today)        67.9       1224.7       68.7       1297.5
  AVX-512 (this CL)     67.6       1325.3       67.0       1282.7

gzip decompression, which verifies a CRC-32, is 8.2% faster (2.8% to
17.5% per file). Compression and the Adler-32 zlib wrapper are within
noise. Compared with the old detection code, the parent CL's checks
cost nothing measurable (1316.1 vs 1325.3 MB/s). Intel CPUs, where
512-bit instructions may lower clocks, have not been measured.

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
---
 third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn b/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
index 29248e1d..b68cf0d9 100644
--- a/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
@@ -226,7 +226,12 @@ source_set("zlib_data_chunk_simd") {
 
 config("zlib_crc32_simd_config") {
   if (use_x86_x64_optimizations) {
-    defines = [ "CRC32_SIMD_SSE42_PCLMUL" ]
+    # The AVX-512 kernel is selected at runtime, only when the CPU and OS
+    # support it, and is compiled through a function target attribute.
+    defines = [
+      "CRC32_SIMD_SSE42_PCLMUL",
+      "CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL",
+    ]
   }
 }
 
